Loaded playbook: consolidate_findings
Description: Sweep notes, per-phase reports, phase logs and artifacts on disk for every finding produced so far, normalise them into one list, and record them to notes so the next phase receives a complete input. Processes one source at a time so context stays bounded. Gathers only - does not test, does not chase new leads.
Mode: agent

╭───────────────────────────────────────────── Starting ─────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ PENTESTAGENT - Non-interactive Mode                                                                │
│                                                                                                    │
│ Target: http://127.0.0.1:5000                                                                      │
│ Model: openai/qwen3.6-27b-fable                                                                    │
│ Mode: Agent                                                                                        │
│ Runtime: Local                                                                                     │
│ Max loops: 40                                                                                      │
│ Task: Sweep notes, per-phase reports, phase logs and artifacts on disk for every finding produced  │
│ so far, normalise them into one list, and record them to notes so the next phase receives a        │
│ complete input. Processes one source at a time so context stays bounded. Gathers only - does not   │
│ test, does not chase new leads.                                                                    │
│                                                                                                    │
│ Phase: Inventory the sources                                                                       │
│ Objective: Build the list of files to process. Do NOT read their contents in this phase.           │
│ Techniques:                                                                                        │
│   1. Read the saved notes for this workspace first - that is the structured record, and it is      │
│ usually incomplete. It is small; reading it whole is fine.                                         │
│   2. List, but do not open: the per-phase reports for this assessment, the phase log files, and    │
│ the artifacts on disk (retrieved binaries, decompiled or unpacked source, captured responses).     │
│   3. Record the artifact paths to notes now, so later phases reuse them rather than fetching       │
│ everything again.                                                                                  │
│   4. Report the file list and their sizes. Anything over about 40 KB must be searched with grep    │
│ rather than read whole in the next phase.                                                          │
│   5. Do NOT cat a log or a report here. The whole point of this phase is to know what exists       │
│ before opening anything.                                                                           │
│                                                                                                    │
│ Phase: Process one source, record, then move on                                                    │
│ Objective: Extract findings from each source individually and write them to notes BEFORE opening   │
│ the next source.                                                                                   │
│ Techniques:                                                                                        │
│   1. Work through the inventory ONE FILE AT A TIME. For each file: extract its findings, write     │
│ them to notes with the notes tool, and only then move to the next file. Never hold two large       │
│ sources at once.                                                                                   │
│   2. READ THE PHASE LOGS. This is the channel nothing else reads and the reason this phase exists. │
│ Search them for evidence that was stated but never recorded: recovered values, decoded output,     │
│ tokens and credentials, status codes that changed, headers observed to be missing, error text, and │
│ any conclusion the assistant narrated about combining two things.                                  │
│   3. Write one note per distinct finding, naming it after the issue rather than the file it came   │
│ from, so the same issue found twice collides instead of duplicating.                               │
│   4. If a source yields nothing, say so and move on. Do not re-read a file you have already        │
│ processed.                                                                                         │
│                                                                                                    │
│ Phase: Normalise into one list                                                                     │
│ Objective: One entry per distinct issue, deduplicated and comparable.                              │
│ Techniques:                                                                                        │
│   1. Produce one entry per distinct issue with: what it is, where it is (endpoint, or file, type   │
│ and member), the evidence observed, whether a control test was run and its result, and the current │
│ proof level.                                                                                       │
│   2. INCLUDE LOW-SEVERITY AND INFORMATIONAL OBSERVATIONS. Missing security headers, permissive     │
│ cross-origin policy, verbose errors and stack traces, exposed metadata and version disclosure are  │
│ routinely dropped between phases precisely because they are individually minor. They belong in the │
│ report, and several of them are also inputs to chaining.                                           │
│   3. Separate what has been demonstrated from what is asserted, and carry that distinction forward │
│ rather than flattening it.                                                                         │
│   4. Build an explicit UNCOMBINED MATERIAL list: every secret, key, token, hash, cookie or opaque  │
│ value held, that has not yet been applied to anything. The next phase needs exactly this list, and │
│ material sitting unused is the most common missed critical.                                        │
│                                                                                                    │
│ Phase: Record to notes                                                                             │
│ Objective: Write the consolidated list down. This is the entire output of the phase - an           │
│ unrecorded finding does not survive to the next one.                                               │
│ Techniques:                                                                                        │
│   1. Record every normalised finding using the notes tool, one note per finding, including its     │
│ evidence and control result. Notes are the only channel later phases reliably receive.             │
│   2. Record the UNCOMBINED MATERIAL list as its own note so the following phase can act on it      │
│ directly.                                                                                          │
│                                                                                                    │
│                                                                                                    │
